From d252dcbe879170a59aaf6d875580c450fd80f621 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: core: do not defer cells missing from a bound layout

of_nvmem_cell_get() returns -EPROBE_DEFER for any cell that a device
with an NVMEM layout does not have, so that consumers wait for a layout
driver that has not probed yet. A layout adds all of its cells while its
driver probes, though, so once it is bound a missing cell will never
appear. A U-Boot environment, for instance, only has cells for the
variables it holds: a consumer of an optional variable that is not set
defers forever instead of going on without it.

Keep deferring while the layout device is not bound and return -ENOENT,
as for a device without a layout, once it is.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
(cherry picked from commit 032dcf1b15785e5b7814f99d438d6aff1d78fa0e)
---
 drivers/nvmem/core.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nvmem/core.c b/drivers/nvmem/core.c
index e4d09e354..83367d7df 100644
--- a/drivers/nvmem/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/core.c
@@ -1476,7 +1476,13 @@ struct nvmem_cell *of_nvmem_cell_get(struct device_node *np, const char *id)
 	of_node_put(cell_np);
 	if (!cell_entry) {
 		nvmem_layout_module_put(nvmem);
-		ret = nvmem->layout ? -EPROBE_DEFER : -ENOENT;
+		/*
+		 * A layout adds all of its cells while its driver probes. Once
+		 * it is bound, a missing cell (an unset U-Boot environment
+		 * variable, for instance) will never appear.
+		 */
+		ret = nvmem->layout && !device_is_bound(&nvmem->layout->dev) ?
+		      -EPROBE_DEFER : -ENOENT;
 		__nvmem_device_put(nvmem);
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	}
